 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "A swamp rabbit attacked the President of the United States.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.863
  },
  {
   "text": "It swam straight at his boat, hissing, teeth bared.",
   "s": 3.163,
   "e": 5.131
  },
  {
   "text": "Jimmy Carter was fishing alone on a pond in Georgia.",
   "s": 5.431,
   "e": 7.952
  },
  {
   "text": "So he grabbed his paddle and splashed it like crazy.",
   "s": 8.252,
   "e": 10.584
  },
  {
   "text": "The rabbit spun around and paddled away, still hissing.",
   "s": 10.884,
   "e": 13.38
  },
  {
   "text": "But back home, nobody believed him. A killer rabbit? Come on.",
   "s": 13.679,
   "e": 16.766
  },
  {
   "text": "Then they found out a White House photographer snapped the whole fight.",
   "s": 17.066,
   "e": 20.024
  },
  {
   "text": "The story leaked to a reporter, and newspapers across America went wild.",
   "s": 20.324,
   "e": 24.092
  },
  {
   "text": "One headline: Bunny Goes Bugs. Rabbit Attacks President.",
   "s": 24.392,
   "e": 27.194
  },
  {
   "text": "And the rabbit? Never caught.",
   "s": 27.494,
   "e": 28.738
  }
 ],
